{
  "description": "#5841 S0.6 — a cross-space move drops each property its target space does not define identically, after the caller acknowledges the losses. The harness space declares `stage` as a select [draft, final]; the space `create_space` makes (`C1`) starts with the editable defaults (`effort`, `url`, `assignee`, …) and is given its own `stage` select with a third option. Moving the page `S1` takes its content blocks `S2` and `S3`, so it would drop `stage` twice (other options) and `effort` once (declared in the target only); `note` is declared in neither space and stays. `S3` is in the Trash when the page moves and goes with it, and a restore after the move brings it back in `C1` (#6080). A move without the acknowledgement, or with a stale one, is refused with `UnacknowledgedPropertyLoss` and writes nothing; the acknowledged one appends the drops before the `space` op. The query steps then read the move back the other way, after the page's blocks took `url` and `assignee` values in `C1` that the harness space does not declare and `S3` went back to the Trash, which still counts. Re-author `expected` / `expected_ops` / `expected_queries` via CONFORMANCE_UPDATE=1.",
